# Paper to read and cite

Huang, P., Lukin, R., Faleev, M. et al. Unveiling the complex structure-property correlation of defects in 2D materials based on high throughput datasets. npj 2D Mater Appl 7, 6 (2023). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41699-023-00369-1

# Dataset contents

A dataset contains 16k structures of 2D materials with point defects, vacancies v(X) and substitutions X(Y).

**High defect concentration dataset:**

1. hBN; v(B), v(N), C(B), C(N)
2. InSe; v(In), V(Se), Ga(In), S(Se)
3. GaSe; v(Ga), v(Se), In(Ga), S(Se)
4. P; v(P), C(P)
5. MoS2; v(Mo), v(S), W(Mo), Se(S)
6. WSe2; v(W), v(Se), Mo(W), S(Se)

Total defect concentrations:
2.5%, 5%, 7.5%, 10%, 12.5%

500 structures per material, 3500 in total

**Low defect concentration dataset**

1. MoS2; v(Mo), v(S), W(Mo), Se(S)
2. WSe2; v(W), v(Se), Mo(W), S(Se)

1 – 3 defects

5934 structures with per material, 11868 in total

